 "steps": [
  {
   "caption": "(a) If one predicate holds everywhere, the disjunction does. Converse: 0 has A, 1 has B, so ∀(A ∨ B) is T, but neither ∀A nor ∀B.",
   "patches": [
    {
     "id": "lawa",
     "set": {
      "tone": "success",
      "fill": "success"
     }
    },
    {
     "id": "wa",
     "set": {
      "hidden": false,
      "tone": "danger"
     }
    },
    {
     "id": "va",
     "set": {
      "hidden": false,
      "text": "converse ✗",
      "tone": "danger"
     }
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "caption": "(b) A common witness witnesses each part. Converse: ∃A and ∃B are T (0 and 1), but no element has both.",
   "patches": [
    {
     "id": "lawb",
     "set": {
      "tone": "success",
      "fill": "success"
     }
    },
    {
     "id": "wb",
     "set": {
      "hidden": false,
      "tone": "danger"
     }
    },
    {
     "id": "vb",
     "set": {
      "hidden": false,
      "text": "converse ✗",
      "tone": "danger"
     }
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "caption": "(c) Modus ponens at every element. Converse: ∀A is F, so ∀A → ∀B is vacuously T; but A(0) → B(0) is T → F.",
   "patches": [
    {
     "id": "lawc",
     "set": {
      "tone": "success",
      "fill": "success"
     }
    },
    {
     "id": "wc",
     "set": {
      "hidden": false,
      "tone": "danger"
     }
    },
    {
     "id": "vc",
     "set": {
      "hidden": false,
      "text": "converse ✗",
      "tone": "danger"
     }
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "caption": "(d) A witness of A is carried to a witness of B. Converse: ∃A → ∃B is T → T, yet A(0) → B(0) fails.",
   "patches": [
    {
     "id": "lawd",
     "set": {
      "tone": "success",
      "fill": "success"
     }
    },
    {
     "id": "wd",
     "set": {
      "hidden": false,
      "tone": "danger"
     }
    },
    {
     "id": "vd",
     "set": {
      "hidden": false,
      "text": "converse ✗",
      "tone": "danger"
     }
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "caption": "(e) Apply (c) both ways. Converse: ∀A and ∀B are both F, so ∀A ↔ ∀B is T; but A(0) ↔ B(0) is F.",
   "patches": [
    {
     "id": "lawe",
     "set": {
      "tone": "success",
      "fill": "success"
     }
    },
    {
     "id": "we",
     "set": {
      "hidden": false,
      "tone": "danger"
     }
    },
    {
     "id": "ve",
     "set": {
      "hidden": false,
      "text": "converse ✗",
      "tone": "danger"
     }
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "caption": "(f) If one A forces all B, each A forces its own B. Converse: ∀(A → B) is T, but ∃A is T and ∀B is F.",
   "patches": [
    {
     "id": "lawf",
     "set": {
      "tone": "success",
      "fill": "success"
     }
    },
    {
     "id": "wf",
     "set": {
      "hidden": false,
      "tone": "danger"
     }
    },
    {
     "id": "vf",
     "set": {
      "hidden": false,
      "text": "converse ✗",
      "tone": "danger"
     }
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "caption": "(g) Pick any element (domains are non-empty). Converse: ∃A is T at 0, ∀A is F at 1.",
   "patches": [
    {
     "id": "lawg",
     "set": {
      "tone": "success",
      "fill": "success"
     }
    },
    {
     "id": "wg",
